                                "sense_id": "b1ad27f7-01e5-3703-a721-80a5fb32fb11",
                                "text": "Every year in California thousands of parents choose names such as José, Andrés and Sofía for their children, often honoring the memory of a deceased grandmother, aunt or sibling. On the state-issued birth certificates, though, those names will be spelled incorrectly."
                            }
